      "sequence_position": 29,
      "problem": "Let $p=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$, $q=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ and $r=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ Find $3p-(q+2r).$",
      "worked_solution": "To compute $3p-(q+2r),$ we just need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3p-(q+2r) & =3\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-([\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]-([\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-12 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
